messages:
maya: Quick FYI — onboarding sample-app blows up when deployed to Cloudflare Workers. Bundled ESM build hits "Error: Cannot find module 'crypto'" at runtime. Anyone else seen the SDK assume Node built-ins?

kevin: Yep. CF Workers are a web runtime (no node: modules). Our SDK still has a few code paths that do `require('crypto')` or import `node:crypto` for hashing/UUIDs. We should publish an ESM runtime entry that uses Web Crypto instead.

sam: Workaround we used in a customer PoC: add an import map + tiny poly that forwards to Web Crypto. Example import map snippet: 

```json
{
  "imports": {
    "node:crypto": "./polyfills/node_crypto_shim.mjs"
  }
}
```

and polyfills/node_crypto_shim.mjs: 

```js
// very small shim: only implements what SDK needs (randomBytes, subtle digest)
export function randomBytes(n){
  const arr = new Uint8Array(n);
  crypto.getRandomValues(arr);
  return arr;
}
export async function sha256(buf){
  const h = await crypto.subtle.digest('SHA-256', buf);
  return new Uint8Array(h);
}
```

kevin: Nice. Also a bundler tip: esbuild/rollup can accidentally leave CJS interop code if you bundle for `node` platform. For workers use `platform: 'neutral'` and `format: 'esm'` so import/exports stay ESM. That avoids runtime `require()` sneaking in.

lisa: Minor TS gotcha we hit: type errors around `globalThis.crypto` if tsconfig libs omit DOM. For Workers use `lib: ["webworker", "es2021"]` (or include `dom` if you need DOM types). Otherwise `crypto.subtle` is missing from the type surface.

maya: Good call. Also the SDK typings expect `Buffer` in a couple helpers — that breaks in Workers. We should provide small runtime helpers in our ESM build that don't rely on Node `Buffer` and instead use `Uint8Array`/TextEncoder.

sam: One more practical note: don't ship huge node built-in polyfills (crypto-browserify, buffer big bundles) — CF Workers enforces script size limits and cold start slows. Prefer tiny shims that call native Web APIs.

kevin: Plan: add `.../dist/sdk.edge.mjs` entrypoint that is ESM-only + minimal runtime shims + docs for "deploying to Cloudflare Workers" including import-map example, wrangler settings, and tsconfig snippet. I'll draft the PR. @maya can you review the sample changes and the README?

maya: Happy to. I'll try to replace Buffer usage and add tests in the sample app.

devex-bot: deploy-bot: preview for sample-app updated — https://preview-sample-app.workers.dev (wrangler dev) :rocket:

sam: FYI: when testing locally with Miniflare, enable `--compatibility-flag=firefox`? (jk) — but seriously, use `miniflare --wrangler` to match the Workers runtime.

kevin: I'll put the doc + PR link in #devex once it's ready. Thanks all :thumbsup:
